Subject: ws2_32: WSALookupServiceBegin semi-stub succeeds with empty set

WSALookupServiceBegin{A,W} were unimplemented FIXME stubs returning
WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY (error 8). Steam's CEF webhelper network_change_notifier
calls WSALookupServiceBeginW; the failure stalled init + spammed cef_log. Return
success with an empty set (Begin->sentinel handle, Next->WSA_E_NO_MORE, End->ok)
so the notifier finishes. Real NLA unimpl; callers see no services (strictly
better than the hard failure). Upstream Wine gap. Verified live: cef_log NLA
errors 6/launch -> 0.

diff --git a/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c b/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
index 915758be886..2fd275ca864 100644
--- a/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
+++ b/dlls/ws2_32/protocol.c
@@ -2232,9 +2232,9 @@ int WINAPI WSAGetServiceClassNameByClassIdW( GUID *class, WCHAR *service, DWORD
  */
 int WINAPI WSALookupServiceBeginA( WSAQUERYSETA *query, DWORD flags, HANDLE *lookup )
 {
-    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) Stub!\n", query, flags, lookup );
-    SetLastError( WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY );
-    return -1;
+    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) semi-stub: returning empty result set\n", query, flags, lookup );
+    *lookup = (HANDLE)(ULONG_PTR)1;
+    return 0;
 }
 
 
@@ -2243,9 +2243,9 @@ int WINAPI WSALookupServiceBeginA( WSAQUERYSETA *query, DWORD flags, HANDLE *loo
  */
 int WINAPI WSALookupServiceBeginW( WSAQUERYSETW *query, DWORD flags, HANDLE *lookup )
 {
-    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) Stub!\n", query, flags, lookup );
-    SetLastError( WSA_NOT_ENOUGH_MEMORY );
-    return -1;
+    FIXME( "(%p %#lx %p) semi-stub: returning empty result set\n", query, flags, lookup );
+    *lookup = (HANDLE)(ULONG_PTR)1;
+    return 0;
 }
 
 
